From d5215d177ab4aeae05e75b1427853ab47bfe42f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:04:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ci: staging contract and functional jobs run the locked
 wrangler

Part of OSE-1695

The T2 and T4 jobs installed the root dependencies only. Root has no
wrangler, so the seed steps' npx wrangler fetched the newest release
(4.151.1 in run 39194783868) while the deploy job ran the locked 4.145.0,
and the unpinned copy ran with CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN_OSE in its environment.

- both jobs install the worker dependencies before their first wrangler step
- that makes them Worker-building jobs, so the hub staging step is now
  required there (continue-on-error removed); the ratchet baseline falls 22 to 20
- a spec requires every job that runs wrangler, directly or through the seed
  and trace scripts, to run the worker npm ci first; red against the old
  workflow on contract-staging-sub and functional-staging-sub

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
